+## PD-018 — Evidence trigger of the Gold v0.2 Alpha rules for runs other than the six the frozen trigger matrix is bound to
+
+- **Status:** `OPEN` — needs the project owner (John). Recorded 2026-10-07, T2 gap closure (round 24).
+- **Source:** `comqutor_alpha/regression/gold_contract_rules.py` executes five rules of John's frozen contract (`v0_2_gold_operational_contract.json`): `NVDA-A101-AI-GROWTH`, `NVDA-A304-VALUATION-RISK`, `MSFT-A102-DIRECT-INFERENCE-TRIGGER` (`must_detect_if_evidence_present`) and the NVDA / AMD growth-vs-valuation composites (`conditional_only`, "any ONE allowed pair"). Their evidence condition ("the defining current-evidence condition is present") was decided once, by reading `structured_agent_outputs.json` of ONE run per ticker, and recorded in `v0_2_evidence_trigger_matrix.json`.
+- **Current handling:** the frozen trigger is used only for the run it is bound to. For any other run (a new Fresh run, a replay, a recovery / re-qualification run, the other saved runs) no approved, executable method determines the trigger, so each rule is `NOT_EVALUABLE` with the Alpha's identification, level and the contract requirement recorded next to it. A historical TRUE/FALSE is never carried over, and the ticker is never a PASS on top of an unevaluated rule.
+- **Decision needed:** how the trigger is to be determined for another run — an approved executable method over the existing evidence authority (ticker-specific, qualified, role-aware, deduplicated fact groups, agent independence, structure support, stance), or a recorded per-run review. Also: the NVDA composite's `evidence_condition` is worded in terms of the component Alphas reaching a detected level, while the matrix and John's Step-4 protocol fix the trigger from evidence independent of the system's output; which reading applies to other runs.
+- **Blocking phase:** none; until decided, a missed Alpha on a new run is recorded as facts and reported `not_evaluable`, not asserted as a FAIL.
+
+## PD-019 — Pair-level `should_detect_if_supported` over `conditional_conflicts`
+
+- **Status:** `OPEN` — needs the project owner (John). Recorded 2026-10-07.
+- **Source:** John's frozen contract defines `should_detect_if_supported` for Alphas / structures (no conflict-pair rule uses it); his frozen baseline (`v0_2_john_frozen_gold_baseline.yaml`) lists the 16 ticker–pair relations as `allowed_main_conflicts`: "ALLOWED structures when supported by evidence -- never mandatory outputs". The label file carries ten of the 16 under `conditional_conflicts` (six from J2 v0.2 task section 8; four moved there by PD-017-REVISED / T2 item 1), and an engine reading of that bucket produced a review item when such a pair had a supporting fact on each side and was not admitted. No approval record backs that reading.
+- **Current handling:** the reading is kept with its result, B2's own rejection reasons and its source, labelled `implementation_only_unapproved`, and decides NO formal status (`diagnostic_findings`). Effect on the saved runs: `docs/audit_artifacts/round_source_linking_t0_t2/round24_t2_gap_closure_20261007/before_after/delta_all_saved_runs.md`. The 16 pairs stay in the buckets they were in; nothing was moved. This overtakes the "open question for John" in the PD-017-REVISED addendum (round 23): SNDK's `pass` no longer depends on moving any pair, because the pair-level reading that produced SNDK's only review item decides nothing.
+- **Decision needed:** whether any conflict pair is an independent detection expectation, and which; if none, whether the ten pairs should stay under `conditional_conflicts` or be carried as `allowed_conflicts`. The composite rules of the contract (NVDA, AMD) are the only conflict-level expectation with a documented basis, and they are executed.
+- **Blocking phase:** none.
+
+## PD-020 — `required_conflicts`: when a pair may be declared required
+
+- **Status:** `OPEN` — needs the project owner (John). Recorded 2026-10-07.
+- **Source:** J2 v0.2 task section 7: `required_conflicts` "only applies to an approved, complete, version-locked reference run; a miss may produce a regression failure". `labels_v2.load_j2_labels_v2` checks pair format, canonicality and mutual exclusivity only; neither it nor the acceptance engine checks that the label is approved or that the evaluated run is the reference run.
+- **Current handling:** no ticker declares a required pair (`required_conflicts` is empty for all six). A required pair is judged from B2's own record: admitted → pass; evaluated and rejected for a recorded reason → not a miss; no usable record → not evaluated (review); only a record that meets every B2 condition and is still not admitted is a miss.
+- **Decision needed:** the approval and reference-run binding a label must carry before `required_conflicts` may be non-empty, and whether the loader must refuse otherwise.
+- **Blocking phase:** none while the list stays empty.
+
+## PD-021 — The other fourteen Gold contract rules
+
+- **Status:** `OPEN` — scope decision. Recorded 2026-10-07.
+- **Source:** the frozen contract has 19 rules; the unified entry executes five (PD-018). The other fourteen — Alpha-level `should_detect_if_supported` / `conditional_only` rules (NVDA-A301, QQQ-A001 / A003 / A304 / A501 / A601, SNDK-A201, MSFT-A101 / A102-indirect / capex-burden), the two negative controls (`QQQ-ETF-CONTEXT-CONTROL`, `SNDK-ANTI-OVER-AI-CONTROL`), `NVDA-SUPPORTING-STRUCTURES` and the TSM transmission composite — are listed in `effective_rules.gold_contract.rules_not_in_effect` and are not evaluated.
+- **Current handling:** a ticker's PASS covers only what the entry executes; `coverage.pass_scope_note` and `release.contract_rules_not_executed` say which contract rules it does not cover. For QQQ and SNDK six and two of those rules are blocking. John's own Step-4 table recorded QQQ run f88c8956 as FAIL (`QQQ-A001-RATE-CUT-CYCLE`); the unified entry shows that run as `pass` precisely because that rule is not executed — the two are not comparable.
+- **Decision needed:** whether and in what order to execute the remaining rules (each needs its trigger from PD-018).
+- **Blocking phase:** any claim that a ticker passes Gold v0.2.
